-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_comments.pcpp - Lexical compliance: comments

  A line comment runs from two slashes to the end of the line, a block
  comment from slash-star to the first star-slash (BNF.md sec 9): block
  comments do not nest, so a slash-star inside one is only text (and a
  warning: lex_comments_err_nested). Two slashes in a string are text.
  (This header is itself a block comment: it never spells those pairs.)

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_comments.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_comments.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    code
    inline
    // not a comment
    between
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    lex_comments_err_unterminated.pcpp
      a block comment never closed (LX0003)
    lex_comments_err_nested.pcpp
      a slash-star inside a block comment: no nesting (LX0203, a warning)
    lex_comments_err_escaped_end.pcpp
      a splice between the * and the / that close a comment (LX0202, a warning)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_comments;

// a line comment
/* a block comment
   over two lines */

begin
  println("code"); // after code
  println(/* inside */ "inline");
  println("// not a comment");
  /* one */ println("between"); /* two */
end.
